{
  "$comment": "Shell commands and how every parser must read them: packages/proxy shell_parse.rs, @intutic/gate shellParse.ts, intutic-clawde gate/shell_parse.py. `parsed` is a list of pipelines, each a list of simple commands: argv after quote removal, and literal, false when a word still holds an expansion or glob, so argv is not exactly what runs. parsed is null when the text is not confidently understood: a redirect, subshell, group, substitution, heredoc, control word, unterminated quote or stray operator. Null is the answer that fails safe: every caller must keep its old behaviour on it. allow lists commandsOutsideAllow cases: `outside` is the commands refused, as written; all of the text when it did not parse or an entry cannot be read. A trailing ` *` allows further arguments; a word that could expand never matches an exact entry.",
